# Frame Demo — Cedar Ridge with the structural post-and-beam frame placed
# automatically by the `frame` directive. Build it to see the bents, ridge, and
# posts drawn over the floor plan:
#   barndsl compile examples/frame_demo.barn --metrics
#   barndsl build   examples/frame_demo.barn --out frame_demo.svg
# See README → "Structure: automatic beam placement".

plan "Frame Demo"
envelope 60 x 40
ceiling 12
note "3 bed / 1 bath with an auto-placed post-and-beam frame."

# Auto post-and-beam frame: bents every <=12 ft along the 60 ft length, each
# spanning the 40 ft width (= the 40 ft single-span limit, so no interior posts),
# with a ridge over the bents. A layout aid — member sizing is the engineer's job.
frame bay 12 span 40 post 6

# --- Open living core (south-west) ---
room great_room: living  at 0,0   size 28 x 26
room dining:     dining   at 28,0  size 18 x 14
room kitchen:    kitchen  at 28,14 size 18 x 12

# --- Shop / garage bay (full-height east) ---
room shop: shop at 46,0 size 14 x 40

# --- Hallway spine ---
room hall: hallway at 0,26 size 46 x 3

# --- Bedrooms + bath (north) ---
room master_bed: bedroom  at 0,29  size 16 x 11
room bed_2:      bedroom  at 16,29 size 12 x 11
room bed_3:      bedroom  at 28,29 size 10 x 11
room bath:       bathroom at 38,29 size 8 x 11

# --- Interior circulation ---
open great_room - dining width 10
open dining - kitchen width 8
open great_room - hall width 4
door hall - master_bed width 2.67
door hall - bed_2 width 2.67
door hall - bed_3 width 2.67
door hall - bath width 2.67

# --- Entrances ---
entry great_room south width 3 offset 20
entry shop south width 10 offset 2 no-egress

# --- Glazing ---
window great_room west width 6 offset 4
window great_room west width 6 offset 16
window great_room south width 8 offset 8
window dining south width 8 offset 2
window master_bed north width 5 offset 5
window bed_2 north width 4 offset 4
window bed_3 north width 4 offset 3
window bath north width 3 offset 2

# --- Covered front porch (outside the envelope) ---
porch front_porch at 0,-8 size 28 x 8 covered
